IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-general`

-- Tests for Part 8, Chapters 1 and 2 (regulations 24 to 28, lines 308 to 352). Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Part 8, Chapters 1 and 2`

§§ `Regulation 24(2): nothing before 6 April 2016 under Chapter 3`

#ASSERT `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (Date 6 4 2016)
#ASSERT `a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (Date 3 4 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (Date 5 4 2016))
#ASSERT NOT (`a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` (Date 3 4 2016))

§§ `Regulation 25(3): the tax year a week falls in`

-- A tax year runs from 6 April to 5 April and is named by the year it begins in.
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 6 4 2026) EQUALS 2026
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS 2026
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS 2026
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 6 4 2016) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 5 4 2016) EQUALS 2015
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 1 5 2020) EQUALS 2020
#ASSERT `the tax year a calendar day falls in` (Date 1 3 2020) EQUALS 2019
-- A week of 5 to 11 April 2026 falls partly in each year: it falls in the year it begins in.
#ASSERT `the tax year a week falls in` (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the tax year a week falls in` (Date 12 4 2026) EQUALS 2026
-- A week of 30 March to 5 April 2026 falls wholly in 2025; a week of 6 to 12 April 2026 wholly in 2026.
#ASSERT `the tax year a week falls in` (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the tax year a week falls in` (Date 6 4 2026) EQUALS 2026

§§ `Regulation 25(1): which Chapter`

#ASSERT `the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` (Date 5 4 2016)
#ASSERT `the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` (Date 1 1 2010)
#ASSERT NOT (`the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` (Date 6 4 2016))
#ASSERT NOT (`the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` (Date 1 1 2030))

§§ `Regulation 25(2): only to the extent necessary`

#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 100 `limited by` 60 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 40 `limited by` 60 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 60 `limited by` 60 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 100 `limited by` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 100 `limited by` (0 MINUS 5) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount the person is credited with` 0 `limited by` 60 EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulations 26 and 27`

-- Only a pre-commencement year, and only where the person would have been entitled on the stated assumptions.
#ASSERT `the person is credited under regulation 26` (Date 1 1 2010) `given` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is credited under regulation 26` (Date 1 1 2010) `given` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is credited under regulation 26` (Date 1 1 2020) `given` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is credited under regulation 27` (Date 4 4 2016) `given` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is credited under regulation 27` (Date 1 1 2020) `given` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is credited under regulation 27` (Date 1 1 2010) `given` FALSE)

§§ `Regulation 28: forces spouses, before 6 April 2016`

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      qef IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A BOOLEAN
      received IS A MAYBE DATE
      form IS A BOOLEAN
      info IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
`a forces spouse` first qef other election received form info MEANS
    `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` WITH
        `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS TRUE
        `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
        `the first day of the week` IS first
        `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS qef
        `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS other
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS election
        `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS received
        `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS form
        `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS info

-- (1) to (3): a week in the year beginning 6 April 2010, the member's earnings factors above the qualifying earnings factor; the
-- application arrives after the week is over (week of 6 to 12 June 2010; received 1 July 2010).
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) TRUE TRUE)
-- (3): a year beginning on or after 6 April 1975 and ending before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 4 1975) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 30 3 1975) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 29 3 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (3): the member's earnings factors must exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (4)(a): not for a week in which the person is entitled to credits under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (4)(b): not for a woman whose reduced rate election is in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (5): no application, no credit.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE))
-- (6): a past period only: received on the last day of the week (12 June) or before is not after the week is over; the day after is.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 12 6 2010)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 13 6 2010)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 6 2010)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (6)(a), (b): the form (or a manner accepted as sufficient) and the information.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2010)) TRUE FALSE))

-- (2)(a) and (b): the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces (or treated so), accompanying the member on an assignment
-- outside the United Kingdom (or treated as doing so).
GIVEN spouse IS A BOOLEAN
      accompanying IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
`a forces spouse who` spouse accompanying MEANS
    `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` WITH
        `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS spouse
        `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS accompanying
        `the first day of the week` IS Date 6 6 2010
        `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS TRUE
        `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS FALSE
        `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS JUST (Date 1 7 2010)
        `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS TRUE
        `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse who` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse who` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` (`a forces spouse who` TRUE FALSE))
